Finding: {"title":"ai-curriculum-gen/structure and module-stream routes bypass aiGateway, have no token-usage recording, and no bound on requested module count","severity":"MEDIUM","area":"Cost control / AI gateway consistency","files":["src/server/routes/routes-ai-curriculum-generator.ts"],"detail":"Unlike every other curriculum AI route (analyzer, export, builder, incremental — all of which call `recordAiTokenUsage`), routes-ai-curriculum-generator.ts calls the Anthropic API directly via raw `fetch` (lines 340-352, 523-541) and never calls `recordAiTokenUsage`. Additionally, `buildStructurePrompt` (lines 80-92) computes `totalModules` from user-supplied `totalFlightHours / flightLessonDurationMin` etc. with no upper bound check before sending the request — a caller supplying a very small `flightLessonDurationMin` (e.g. 1) with a large `totalFlightHours` can request an enormous number of modules, and since Phase 2 (module-stream) is called once per module from the client in a loop, this multiplies into many uncapped, unmetered Claude API calls.","impact":"Token spend for this specific curriculum-generation flow is invisible to whatever admin dashboard/reporting consumes `recordAiTokenUsage` data, undercounting real AI cost. Combined with the missing bound on module count, a malformed or malicious payload (e.g. `flightLessonDurationMin: 1`, `totalFlightHours: 1000`) could trigger thousands of individual Claude calls from the client loop with no server-side cap.","recommendation":"Route these calls through `aiGateway` like the sibling routes for consistent metering, add `recordAiTokenUsage` calls using the response's `usage` data, and add a sanity cap on computed `totalModules` (e.g. reject or clamp above ~150) in buildStructurePrompt / the /structure route handler before calling Claude.","confidence":"medium"}
